WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-24, with W22 (0.3.2)


STATE

  Version 0.3.2, Phase P4 in progress (process substitution and **
  recursive globbing), on branch dev. 0.3.2 adds:
  - process substitution <(...) and >(...) through /dev/fd in
    include/tam-clam/ast.h, include/tam-clam/lex.h, src/lex.c,
    src/expand.c, src/exec.c, src/shell.c, and src/lint.c: parent pipe
    fds held above fd 10 (without CLOEXEC so external commands inherit
    /dev/fd/N), sibling procsub fds closed in children to prevent EOF
    deadlocks, and automatic per-command fd close + child reaping;
  - ** recursive globbing (off by default for strict POSIX
    compatibility, enabled via `shopt -s globstar` or `set -o globstar`)
    in src/glob.c, src/options.c, src/builtins.c, and src/builtins_cmd.c:
    supports **/*.ext, **/, trailing **, deduplication, hidden-entry
    exclusion, and symlink-loop immunity (lstat);
  - tests/test_procsub.c (20 checks), expanded tests/test_glob.c (32
    checks), tests/spec/procsub.test.sh (6 cases),
    tests/spec/globstar.test.sh (7 cases, all verified against
    bash --posix), fuzz seeds, and sandbox/demo-0.3.2-procsub-globstar.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test, make sanitize, and make
  fuzz pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  arch/keys.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default; ** recursive globbing is off by default.


